\boxed{ 144 \text{ m}^3 } 
The volume of the rectangular pool is given by the product of its length, width, and depth.  Given that length = 12 m, width = 6 m, and depth = 4 m, the total volume of the pool is:
Volume = length × width × depth = 12 m × 6 m × 4 m = 288 m³
Since the pool is half full, the volume of the water in the pool is half of the total volume:
Volume of water = (1/2) × Volume = (1/2) × 288 m³ = 144 m³

